      "body": "\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe TP cases in SGLang UT needs to remove the hard-coded code to accommodate SPR.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Added adaptive allocation logic for TPs (Tensor Parallelism) to specific NUMA node CPUs; regardless of TP settings, execution is confined to the CPUs of the given NUMA nodes.\r\n- Bypassed automatic threshold setting to prevent small models from crashing due to memory exhaustion on a single physical node.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n- When started as a single process, the workload runs on the given NUMA nodes if TP > 1.\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35949492818](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35949492818)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35949492622](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35949492622)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35949492932](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35949492932)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
